  "vegSub": "MVS 9 · Eucalyptus woodland with a tussock grass understorey · in Victoria's terms, Grassy Woodland / Valley Grassy Forest (EVC 175 / 47), Gippsland Plain",
  "intro": "Before 1750 your address in Ivanhoe East stood on the gentle rises above the Yarra River, in grassy woodland of Yellow Box, Red Box and River Red Gum over a tussocky floor of Kangaroo Grass, Grey Tussock-grass and wallaby grasses, with wattles, Cherry Ballart and Sweet Bursaria scattered through it and lilies, peas and daisies flowering between the tussocks in spring. Like most of Melbourne's grassy woodlands it has been almost entirely cleared, so bringing it back to a garden genuinely matters. The plants below are indigenous to it and grouped by the layer they fill. Plant the canopy first; the shrubs, lilies and grasses belong in the dappled light beneath it. For your exact Victorian vegetation class, look up your address at findmyevc.com.",
